  "headline": "Tony Loses the Trade, Wins the Championship",
  "publicationDraft": "Tony traded injured George Kittle and recently recovered Jarvis Landry for Kyle Pitts, fresh off consecutive 100-yard games. Kuhl could afford the gamble with Travis Kelce already in his lineup. Kittle returned and erupted for 63.70 points across Weeks 13–14, while Pitts scored only one NFL touchdown all season. Yet Pitts delivered 13.20 in Tony’s 4.30-point championship victory; Kittle managed 3.10 that week. A straight swap would have cost Tony the title, although starting Waddle or Brown instead of Lamb could have rescued him. Kuhl got the stronger observed return, but Tony’s acquisition delivered at exactly the right damn moment.",
